{"repositoryId":134980773,"availability":"available","full":"citelab/gini","name":"gini","description":"GINI Is Not Internet - A toolkit for constructing virtual micro Internet","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":17,"forks":8,"created":"2018-05-26T17:16:50Z","updated":"2026-10-15T13:05:24Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://citelab.github.io/gini/","topics":[],"demo":"https://citelab.github.io/gini/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:36.628Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:36.628Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:36.628Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:36.628Z","stars":17,"forks":8}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A visual lab for computer networks, cloud computing, and operating systems — draw a system, press Run, and it comes to life as real containers (and a real xv6 kernel) you can inspect, drive, and observe.","💬 Join the community: GINI Discord — questions, help, and discussion.","GINI lets students and instructors build a topology on a canvas, then launches it as honest, running infrastructure on Docker: a real C router that actually forwards packets, a real OpenFlow controller programming a real switch, and real cloud services (databases, object stores, message queues, dashboards) discoverable by name — plus a real xv6 operating-system kernel you can watch and extend in a visual Machine Lab. A built-in AI tutor — GINI — explains what's on the canvas, animates how packets flow, and can scaffold whole working systems from a one-line description."],"features":["Computer Networks — switches, routers, subnets, firewalls, and real OpenFlow SDN.","Cloud Computing — VPC-style networking, managed services, autoscaling, observability.","Operating Systems — a real xv6 (RISC-V) kernel in a visual Machine Lab: watch the","Visual builder — a fast PySide6/Qt 6 canvas with a searchable palette of 40","networking and cloud elements, theming, save/load, and an inspector."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/citelab/gini/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"44b3e94462bd43bbaf1b09656e4efd8f817e8e9e44e290d173bfd74fc5a5a6f4","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:36.769Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:36.769Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A visual lab for computer networks, cloud computing, and operating systems — draw a system, press Run, and it comes to life as real containers (and a real xv6 kernel) you can inspect, drive, and observe.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/citelab/gini/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Right-click any node for Open console, Log in, View logs, or Delete.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/citelab/gini/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Full detail — the release guards and why each exists, GHCR login, the QEMU fallback — is in scripts/README.md.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/citelab/gini/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"44b3e94462bd43bbaf1b09656e4efd8f817e8e9e44e290d173bfd74fc5a5a6f4","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/citelab/gini/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:36.769Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T13:05:24Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/citelab/gini/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:36.770Z","hash":"44b3e94462bd43bbaf1b09656e4efd8f817e8e9e44e290d173bfd74fc5a5a6f4","originalBytes":17521,"storedBytes":17521,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["gini","install","podman","scripts","real","docker","gbuilder","container","engine","run","bash","machine","pip","gini-toolkit","grouter","kernel","one","openflow","sudo","app","cloud","dev.sh","first","images","mode","model","xv6","build","gini-core","networking","running","services","setup","tests","tutor","what","colima","controller","docs","each","lab","launch","open","pipx","pypi","python","readme.md","registry","